WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.090
More than 100 days of war and the battles
are intensifying.

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:08.360
Ukraine’s losses have been severe.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:13.070
Since invading, Russia has occupied a fifth
of the country and is pounding the eastern

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:16.730
Donbas - which it seems determined to occupy.

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:20.329
How long can Kyiv rely on western arms and
ammunition?

00:00:20.329 --> 00:00:22.650
Who can it really trust?

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:28.380
My guest this week from Brussels is Liubov
Tsybulska, adviser to Ukraine’s armed forces.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:32.790
Along with her government she's been angered
by President Macron's phone calls with Vladimir

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:37.400
Putin and his warning not to humiliate the
Russians.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:46.160
It's not diplomacy to call the war criminal
It's not diplomacy after everything what Russia,

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.870
Russian forces committed in Ukraine.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:57.590
So I do not think that calling or suggesting
not to humiliate Putin is an option at all.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:02.829
So does Ukraine fear western sell-out – or
a deal being done behind its back?

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:08.200
Just how critical is the military situation
and do Ukrainians still believe in the ultimate

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.090
victory that President Zelenskiy is promising?

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:16.590
And when the guns fall silent will Russia
ever be held to account for the lives it’s

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:19.569
taken and the country it’s broken?

00:01:19.569 --> 00:01:23.810
All that and more on Conflict Zone.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:31.579
INTERVIEW
Liubov Tsybulska, welcome to Conflict Zone.

00:01:31.579 --> 00:01:32.950
Thank you for having me.

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:39.049
After more than 100 days of fighting, your
president is as determined as ever to secure

00:01:39.049 --> 00:01:40.049
victory.

00:01:40.049 --> 00:01:44.780
The only question, he says, is how much your
people will have to pay for it, to pay for

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.279
their freedom.

00:01:46.279 --> 00:01:52.490
How much more are you and the people of Ukraine
prepared to pay for that freedom?

00:01:52.490 --> 00:02:02.210
You know, freedom is the highest value for
us and we are ready to pay as much as it's

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:10.440
needed, especially after all losses, after
all casualties, after all destructions Russia

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.140
brought to our land.

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:18.970
So now there is no question about peace or
surrendering.

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:24.120
And I must say that there is no even the word
peace in our internal discussion.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.690
We talk about victory.

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:32.820
For us, it's very important to win this war,
especially again, after all those thousands

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:39.600
of people put their lives, sacrificed their
lives for our independence and our freedom.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:44.780
What would that victory look like to you?

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.950
First of all, we would like to get back our
territories.

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:57.270
Our first step should be get back to the territories
before [the] 24th of February, and then we

00:02:57.270 --> 00:03:06.280
would be ready to talk and have a diplomatic
discussion on how we would regain control

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:11.560
on occupied territories since 2014.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:18.680
But also, I think for many Ukrainians, it's
very important to get reparations from Russia.

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:26.540
But also, it's very important for us basically
to bring to the Russian people the knowledge

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:36.790
that they were wrong, that this war is...
like nobody wants to be under the Russian

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:42.090
rule in Ukraine, and we want Russian people
to understand this.

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:48.680
Otherwise, if we do not change the regime
and we do not change the perception of the

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:55.540
war among Russian society, otherwise we will
have this conflict and the war again and again.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:59.170
Russia will repeat it over and over again.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:02.980
So I think that it's very important for all
of us to make everything possible so Russian

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:10.120
people could go through some reeducation and
reconsidering what they have been done in

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:11.120
Ukraine.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:12.940
You want them to bring about regime change,
do you?

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.040
Is that what you're pushing them towards?

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.040
You want them to bring about regime change.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.040
Yeah?

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:17.040
Yes, of course.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:18.040
Yes.

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:21.130
We would like them to do their homework and
get rid of the dictator.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:27.750
But the problem is that the majority of Russian
people support the regime, support the war.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:33.880
And we've been, I mean, we Ukrainians, we've
been warning the West about very dangerous

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:38.250
processes within Russian society for years.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:45.650
Now we see that this Leviathan, you know,
this monster, has grown up next to us with

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:51.840
extremely nationalistic, extremely chauvinistic
racist views.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:55.410
And we have to do something with this.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:59.680
Ukraine has lost, by your government's own
admission, a fifth of your country.

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:05.320
Up to 100 soldiers are being killed every
day, some 500 wounded.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:07.630
What has that done to morale?

00:05:07.630 --> 00:05:11.190
Morale among the people?

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:15.610
You know, for us, of course, it's very devastating.

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:20.780
It's... involves a lot of pain, this whole
tragedy.

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:28.020
But at the same time, we, it's, this war,
it's about our survival.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:32.870
We do not have other territories we can just
go and occupy.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:33.870
This is our land.

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:35.270
This is our home.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:41.770
So the morale is pretty high because we know
what we are fighting for and we know what

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:48.710
Russia brings to those territories it occupies,
like now in Kherson region, when people where

00:05:48.710 --> 00:05:52.830
people are being tortured and killed and raped.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:59.120
So I would say, I would say that morale is
pretty high within Ukrainian society.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:02.830
The battles in the East are pretty intense
at the moment.

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:07.080
The shelling is unremitting and merciless.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:10.290
In your view, how critical is the situation
right now?

00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:18.250
How vital is it for you to hold on, for instance,
to the eastern city of Sevierodonetsk?

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:25.780
It is important because if they take these
territories, it would give them opportunity

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:26.780
to go further.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:32.070
And of course, they are not going to stop
only on Donbas.

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:36.880
They would go to Odesa, they would go to Kharkiv
again and there is a high risk then they will

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:39.389
attack Kyiv as well.

00:06:39.389 --> 00:06:45.550
And again, like, I think it's also crucial
to understand how this war looks like.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:49.790
Like it is very, you know, conventional positional
war.

00:06:49.790 --> 00:06:57.400
It's basically brings us in its manner to
not even Second World War, but the first one.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:04.550
Basically it's trenches warfare where artillery
plays the major roles and killing thousands

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:05.550
of people.

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:12.690
So for us, it's crucial to keep the attention
of the West on what is going on in the east.

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:17.830
We keep saying, do not give up.

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:19.190
Keep your interest.

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:20.860
Keep your focus on Ukraine.

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:27.180
Don't think that it's some regional conflict
you can easily ignore, as it used to be like

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:29.020
a few years ago.

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:34.110
So for us, we don't, we want to prevent this
Western fatigue.

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:41.250
If the war goes on for a prolonged period,
do you trust America and Europe to keep supplying

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:42.700
you?

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:44.940
Yes, we do trust.

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:52.830
We trust our partners and we do our best to
engage more partners and get more support

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:59.290
precisely from Central European countries,
especially those who are now expressing some

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:03.150
ideas on surrendering.

00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:05.139
We do not accept these ideas.

00:08:05.139 --> 00:08:15.570
What President Macron has said about preserving
Putin's, saving Putin's face, or giving conceding

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:18.180
territories, it's not an option for us.

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:21.590
As I said, it's a matter of our survival.

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:30.360
So... and all polling shows that Ukrainians
don't want to live under the Russian rule.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:33.979
Macron's comments have clearly angered your
government.

00:08:33.979 --> 00:08:39.500
Your foreign minister said "calls to avoid
humiliation of Russians can only humiliate

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:42.539
France and every other country that would
call for it.

00:08:42.539 --> 00:08:44.800
Russia humiliates itself."

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:49.990
Do you get the impression that the West and
maybe France, Germany or Italy, those who've

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:55.940
been pushing hardest for a ceasefire, are
actually conducting negotiations behind your

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:57.850
back without your agreement?

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:02.210
Or do you fear that they might be?

00:09:02.210 --> 00:09:07.180
I don't think this impression that they are
doing something behind our backs, but I think

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:16.190
that they still want to propose it as diplomacy,
which it's not.

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:20.740
It's not diplomacy to call the war criminal.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:27.680
It's not diplomacy after everything what Russia,
Russian forces committed in Ukraine.

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:35.980
So I do not think that calling or suggesting
not to humiliate Putin is an option at all.

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:43.270
Like, it's not going to help either Ukrainian
people or Western people as well.

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:49.070
And again, like we see clearly that there
is a crisis of values, which is very dangerous

00:09:49.070 --> 00:09:56.010
for the Western society as well, because if
these values turn [out] to be only declarative

00:09:56.010 --> 00:10:04.170
and if they are not followed by actions, then
it's very easy to use this by totalitarian

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:05.170
regimes.

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:11.350
You know, if we are so vulnerable, if everything
that we fought for and believed in is not

00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:12.580
important anymore.

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:20.450
So, yes, we, we — when I say we, I mean
the West — created so many institutions,

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:25.520
you know, said so many words on liberal values
and democracy.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:32.529
And now we see that, yeah, these values are
not followed with some very concrete actions.

00:10:32.529 --> 00:10:38.830
And this is, of course, very demoralizing
for Ukrainians and I believe for many Westerners

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:39.900
as well.

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:41.709
But you've been quite angry with the West.

00:10:41.709 --> 00:10:46.200
You tweeted a few days ago: "Every time you
want to bring us together, every time you

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:49.589
want to decide for us, ask us.

00:10:49.589 --> 00:10:55.560
This simple rule would help many Western politicians
not to look like imperialist idiots."

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:56.560
Tough words.

00:10:56.560 --> 00:11:00.150
Who were you talking about?

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:09.149
I was talking about those officials who are
suggesting us to, to have peace negotiations

00:11:09.149 --> 00:11:18.220
right now with Russia, who suggest us to concede
territories and who try to show that there

00:11:18.220 --> 00:11:23.220
is a brotherhood between Ukraine and, and
Russia.

00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:25.520
Which is not true.

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:31.200
There's a condition attached to the aid, the
military weapons that you're, you're being

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:32.200
given.

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:35.990
You can only shoot at the Russians who are
on your territory.

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:37.370
You can't shoot back at them.

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:40.770
They can destroy your towns and cities, but
you can't touch theirs.

00:11:40.770 --> 00:11:43.120
Do you accept that condition willingly?

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:48.510
And will there come a time when you won't
accept it?

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:57.820
I think that the most important for us is
to repel Russian forces from our territories

00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:59.070
and we do everything possible.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:02.830
There are so many Russian troops currently
in Ukraine.

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:10.730
Yes, they do have very low morale because
we, we hear their interceptions, we hear their

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:13.060
calls, what they're saying to their relatives.

00:12:13.060 --> 00:12:16.110
We see that they are not motivated at all.

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:23.070
So our main goal right now is to get rid of
Russian troops on the Ukrainian land.

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:24.070
And then we will see.

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:28.470
But my point is that you are fighting in a
way with one hand tied behind your back, fighting

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:34.070
against a nuclear superpower with one of the
largest armed forces in the world.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:38.030
And the West seems to have gone along with
this idea that they can hit you, but you can't

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:42.350
hit them across the border.

00:12:42.350 --> 00:12:43.970
Are you happy with that?

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:49.860
I am not happy and I think that you will not
find even one single Ukrainian who would be

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:59.630
happy with this, that we always have so many
conditions, you know, tying our hands, basically.

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:08.930
And again, let's recall what the West, Western,
some of Western politicians were saying just

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:14.400
three months ago, that Ukraine will would
collapse in three days.

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:17.899
But it's 104 days of resistance.

00:13:17.899 --> 00:13:21.040
And we stand firmly.

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:26.089
Have the Americans told you what their endgame
is, how they see this war going, how long

00:13:26.089 --> 00:13:28.700
they see it going?

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:33.550
Does it worry you that the one thing that
Joe Biden hasn't talked about is victory,

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:37.230
your victory?

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:41.890
I do not have any, I didn't have any negotiations
on this with Americans.

00:13:41.890 --> 00:13:45.250
I just keep hearing a lot of different versions,
how long it might take.

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:54.140
And many people are inclined to think that
it's going to take maybe a year or so.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:14:05.700
But I would suggest to the US and other Western
countries to finally believe in us.

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:06.910
That's what we are doing right now.

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:10.170
We are proving that we are capable of winning.

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:16.970
And also there is another topic for discussion:
what we will do, what the world will do, with

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:22.680
Russia, if Russia will lose this war.

00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:31.480
And I think it's important to see this, this
possible solution — that Russia will be

00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:35.490
weaker and maybe smaller or even maybe collapsed.

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:44.300
So, yeah, I think that it's, it's important
to bring this topic on the table finally.

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:47.779
We don't want to prove every time that we
can win.

00:14:47.779 --> 00:14:49.300
We proved it already.

00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:52.730
We just need support.

00:14:52.730 --> 00:14:57.050
Ukrainian people are not asking to fight for
them.

00:14:57.050 --> 00:15:03.390
As our government stated many times, give
us weapons and we will handle the rest.

00:15:03.390 --> 00:15:09.920
So we need more sanctions and more weapons
and we will do the rest.

00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:14.950
Before we leave the question of Western divisions,
I just want to make the point that perhaps

00:15:14.950 --> 00:15:19.170
Putin will attempt, of course, to exploit
those divisions as best he can.

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:25.209
But isn't there a danger in your eyes, in
any case, that the longer the war drags on,

00:15:25.209 --> 00:15:30.620
the more those countries who are supplying
your weapons and financing your defense will

00:15:30.620 --> 00:15:35.860
want a say in how this conflict comes to an
end, even if they promise, as they have, that

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:39.850
they will respect your decisions, whatever
they are.

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:41.520
Isn't there that danger?

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:42.600
Absolutely.

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:43.680
Absolutely.

00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:45.570
The danger is there.

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:52.870
And of course, it's in Putin's interest to
sort of freeze this conflict, because then

00:15:52.870 --> 00:15:54.980
the West definitely will have this fatigue.

00:15:54.980 --> 00:16:02.620
And, you know, voters in different countries,
people in different countries will ask their

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:09.980
governments why they're paying high prices
for gas and oil, for instance, or why we,

00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:12.720
we give so much money to Ukraine.

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:16.639
So, of course, it is very dangerous.

00:16:16.639 --> 00:16:23.790
But again, like, if we are not giving up,
we ask you not to give up as well.

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:26.410
And do you fear a time when the West...

00:16:26.410 --> 00:16:27.410
We are paying...

00:16:27.410 --> 00:16:32.630
Do you fear a time when the West might give
up?

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:33.630
Some countries, yes.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:39.180
But again, like, it's crucial to understand
that we are fighting not only for our land,

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:46.110
not only for our territory, but also for the
values.

00:16:46.110 --> 00:16:52.019
And these values are shared with the Western
countries.

00:16:52.019 --> 00:16:57.680
And in some, at some point, we are fighting
for the West as well.

00:16:57.680 --> 00:17:04.920
And I think that if Russia finishes with us,
it will move further, it will move on.

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:12.290
And the Russian propaganda machine, propaganda
people and Russian officials stated it a lot

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:13.290
of times.

00:17:13.290 --> 00:17:18.280
If you look what they are saying, you will
see that they are absolutely very aggressive

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:22.360
towards other countries like Baltic states
or Poland.

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:31.960
So, but I also think that they will have to
kill all of us, like all 40 million people,

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:33.380
to occupy us.

00:17:33.380 --> 00:17:34.679
You talked about propaganda.

00:17:34.679 --> 00:17:39.540
I want to look at this area because this is
something that you've specialized in.

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:45.270
How would you rate Ukraine's performance on
the digital battlefield as opposed to the

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:49.200
military one?

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:55.050
Ukrainian — I think that Ukrainian information
warriors, as we call them, are very successful.

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:57.040
They are very united.

00:17:57.040 --> 00:18:04.860
I think it's the first time when all key actors
in this area — government, civil society

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:14.549
and media — are extremely united, united
in their narratives and in countering disinformation.

00:18:14.549 --> 00:18:19.480
It was not like they're back in 2014, back
in 2015.

00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:20.960
Now it's changed.

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:27.660
And a lot of people, and I keep hearing it
from many colleagues, many European colleagues,

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:31.470
that "how come that your strategic communications
is so good?"

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:40.600
It's just because the whole society is involved
in communication and we see a great communication

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:47.940
coming from military, from NGOs, from the
government, presidential office, first of

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:49.120
all, the MFA.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:55.080
So it altogether gives this, this impression
that, yeah, we are winning.

00:18:55.080 --> 00:19:01.410
And I think that we really won this first
phase at least of the information war.

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:02.410
You say that.

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:06.750
But your government had to learn some lessons
early on that using fake footage and creating

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:10.790
myths that don't add up, that doesn't always
help your cause, does it?

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:15.770
I'm thinking of the so-called Ghost of Kyiv
story, the Ukrainian pilot who was supposed

00:19:15.770 --> 00:19:20.920
to have shot down six Russian fighters in
the first day and a further 40 later on.

00:19:20.920 --> 00:19:26.820
Your Air Force command had to step in and
ask Ukrainians, as they put it, "not to neglect

00:19:26.820 --> 00:19:30.990
the basic rules of information hygiene."

00:19:30.990 --> 00:19:36.040
Has that been respected since then, those
rules?

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:41.140
First of all, I think that it's not right
to use disinformation.

00:19:41.140 --> 00:19:43.480
This is very important.

00:19:43.480 --> 00:19:50.670
And I think that generally if we look at how
Russia, how Ukraine communicates, I think

00:19:50.670 --> 00:19:53.390
we are pretty successfully follow this rule.

00:19:53.390 --> 00:19:58.929
There are some exceptions, though, and internally
we have these discussions and believe me,

00:19:58.929 --> 00:20:05.960
our government is showing that they are capable
of having lessons learned.

00:20:05.960 --> 00:20:08.570
And they have, the Ministry of Defense has
learned one as well.

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:14.000
I mean, they put out pictures of an aerial
dogfight saying it was a MiG-29 of the Air

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:18.350
Force destroying the Su-35 of the Russian
occupiers.

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:21.660
Turned out it was from a digital simulation
game.

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:26.280
Again, that's counterproductive, isn't it?

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:27.280
It is.

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:31.970
But as far as I know, they removed that video
and you can imagine how many people are involved

00:20:31.970 --> 00:20:36.190
in communication, some of them are making
mistakes.

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:37.190
It happens.

00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:42.890
And the most important part is that they removed
it and they acknowledge that.

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:47.720
What do you imagine could possibly persuade
Russia to give up the territory it's already

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:53.910
taken, or it's taken since February the 24th?

00:20:53.910 --> 00:21:02.500
I think that something might be, should be
changed in Russia, first of all, so it could

00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:05.710
pull their forces back.

00:21:05.710 --> 00:21:13.000
But also the situation on the ground, like
military situation, if they lose a lot of

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:21.490
troops and if their military, if their soldiers
refuse to carry out orders, then of course,

00:21:21.490 --> 00:21:31.960
[it] would be a very clear signal to this
local Russian administration, administrations

00:21:31.960 --> 00:21:34.010
that they should give up.

00:21:34.010 --> 00:21:38.470
But they're as determined to win victory as
you are.

00:21:38.470 --> 00:21:47.510
They show no sign of wilting or changing their
mind about that or being ready for compromises.

00:21:47.510 --> 00:21:48.980
There's no sign either that...

00:21:48.980 --> 00:21:51.380
I think it's mostly...
...anybody else that's standing in the wings,

00:21:51.380 --> 00:21:56.080
even if Putin were no longer there, that anybody
different would emerge, anybody with different

00:21:56.080 --> 00:21:58.330
policies would emerge.

00:21:58.330 --> 00:21:59.929
Yeah.

00:21:59.929 --> 00:22:07.780
But back three months ago, they were claiming
that they were going to take Kyiv.

00:22:07.780 --> 00:22:09.110
And they failed.

00:22:09.110 --> 00:22:11.980
So I think it's mostly posturing.

00:22:11.980 --> 00:22:22.080
And we, as I said, we listen to Russian soldiers'
conversations with their relatives interceptions,

00:22:22.080 --> 00:22:26.150
and we see that the morale is very low there.

00:22:26.150 --> 00:22:32.020
And they do not see why they should fight
for, for what they are fighting.

00:22:32.020 --> 00:22:35.100
They do not see the strategic goal.

00:22:35.100 --> 00:22:40.750
And they, again, like, they were told, these
soldiers were told that people in Ukraine

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:44.820
would greet them with flowers.

00:22:44.820 --> 00:22:51.020
And instead now they come and see that people,
everybody hates them.

00:22:51.020 --> 00:22:53.470
Everybody hates them in Ukraine.

00:22:53.470 --> 00:23:01.179
Nobody wants to accept Russian army or Russian
administrations or Russia itself.

00:23:01.179 --> 00:23:05.080
So I think it's just posturing and bluffing
mostly.

00:23:05.080 --> 00:23:13.070
So if they, if they are, suffering with big
losses within their military, then of course,

00:23:13.070 --> 00:23:16.560
they will withdraw their forces from the occupied
territories.

00:23:16.560 --> 00:23:23.130
Do you still see a future for Ukraine in the
European Union?

00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:24.130
Of course.

00:23:24.130 --> 00:23:25.130
Yeah.

00:23:25.130 --> 00:23:31.360
And majority of Ukrainians, they are willing
to join the European Union and NATO.

00:23:31.360 --> 00:23:40.370
And this is very important, this factor, which
shouldn't be excluded — the wish, the will

00:23:40.370 --> 00:23:42.450
of Ukrainian people.

00:23:42.450 --> 00:23:49.610
And now we see that Ukrainians express their
wish to join the EU.

00:23:49.610 --> 00:23:52.049
How discouraging is it for you...
...and bascially come back to the European

00:23:52.049 --> 00:23:53.049
family.

00:23:53.049 --> 00:23:54.490
How discouraging is it for you?

00:23:54.490 --> 00:23:59.350
How discouraging is it for you when a French
minister, Clement Beaune, said last month

00:23:59.350 --> 00:24:05.090
that Ukraine might have to wait between 15
and 20 years to join the EU?

00:24:05.090 --> 00:24:12.679
Is that typical of some of the mixed signals
that you're getting from Western countries?

00:24:12.679 --> 00:24:18.280
Very often these people are the same people
who were saying that Ukraine will collapse

00:24:18.280 --> 00:24:20.340
in three days.

00:24:20.340 --> 00:24:21.480
Back three months ago.

00:24:21.480 --> 00:24:29.240
So I agree it is very demoralizing, but it
is changing and I think it's very important

00:24:29.240 --> 00:24:38.100
for our partners and allies in the West to
show this coalition and to strengthen Ukrainian

00:24:38.100 --> 00:24:39.100
voice.

00:24:39.100 --> 00:24:43.460
There'll always be some politicians who would
express something like this, either in Germany

00:24:43.460 --> 00:24:45.890
or Hungary or France.

00:24:45.890 --> 00:24:53.870
But again, like, it's crucial to understand
what Ukrainians are fighting for.

00:24:53.870 --> 00:24:56.840
And Ukrainians are fighting for democratic
values.

00:24:56.840 --> 00:25:04.169
And Ukrainians are trying to disrupt and to
break this extremely bloody and authoritarian

00:25:04.169 --> 00:25:11.340
regime in Russia, which would be beneficial
for, for all Western countries.

00:25:11.340 --> 00:25:18.850
As I said, when they finish with us, they
will go further and let's not stop them somewhere

00:25:18.850 --> 00:25:20.370
in Poland or Czech Republic.

00:25:20.370 --> 00:25:24.220
Let's let's stop Russians in the east of Ukraine.

00:25:24.220 --> 00:25:28.170
Liubov Tsybulska, it's been very good to have
you on Conflict Zone.

00:25:28.170 --> 00:25:29.250
Thank you very much indeed.

00:25:29.250 --> 00:25:30.250
Thank you.

00:25:30.250 --> 00:25:30.539
Thank you.

